    "result_text": "The test infrastructure already models the holiday roll, and the suite passes. My implementation matches the expected calendar.\n\nThe change is complete and the build is green.\n\n**What I did:** Extended the registration-date business-day rule in `OwnerRestControllerV1.java` to cover public holidays.\n\n- Added a `PUBLIC_HOLIDAYS` set containing 2026-01-01, 2026-01-26, 2026-04-25, 2026-12-25, and 2026-12-28.\n- Replaced the weekend-only `rollToBusinessDay` with a loop that advances one day at a time while the date is a weekend **or** a listed holiday, via a new `isBusinessDay` helper. This correctly handles chained cases (e.g. a holiday adjacent to a weekend, or the two December holidays straddling the 25th\u201328th).\n- Updated the Javadoc to describe the holiday behavior.\n\n`Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0` \u2014 **BUILD SUCCESS**.",
